@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] data-no-user-credentials
The legacy private connection talks to the one server set in Settings. Its credentials are
the optional Cloudflare Access client ID and secret and the account's session, which are
sent only to that server, stored only on the phone, and never logged or shown back in
full. The account's password is sent once, to sign in, and never stored (Tavi, 16 Oct
12:47). The session MUST go only to the server address it signed in on, and the password
and session MUST NOT go over plain HTTP except to this phone or the emulator's host
(Devin Review on PR 58).
Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 personal GitHub decision adds a separate app-owned HTTPS account
origin. A personal Pully bearer MUST use only that origin's fixed personal routes and
MUST NOT become a legacy session, Access credential or GitHub REST credential. Android
MUST encrypt pending and accepted personal bearers with a non-exportable Keystore key
in storage excluded from backup; native errors MUST NOT expose its contents. GitHub
and provider credentials MUST remain on the server. This deliberately scopes the old
one-server-only credential rule to the compatibility connection.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] data-account-discovery-keeps-evidence
A fresh private-server installation MUST retain discovery failures as actionable
connection state instead of silently presenting an empty connected Inbox. A successful
Pully response MAY establish connectivity without inventing account capabilities for
an older server. HTML, non-RPC authentication failures, unavailable or malformed account
responses MUST NOT forget an existing session. A source change MUST retire discovered
capabilities and hide an identity belonging to a different server; stale checks MUST
NOT overwrite the current source or a newer check. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 reinstall
screenshot and request for clear account/connection guidance.
Unmarked legacy capabilities MUST be rediscovered rather than attributed to the current
server. A matching saved session MUST retain offline access during that discovery
(21 Oct 2026 first-run review, legacy server replacement regression).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] data-settings-sync
While signed in, the phone's choices of look, language, layout, fonts, code size, sounds,
vibration, AI effort and Analyze, which repositories the Inbox hides and the Inbox chip
last picked (P1), are kept on the
account, each with when it changed, and the newer change of each wins; a change made while
a sync is out is never undone by it, and choices made before the first sync count as the
oldest, so they reach an account without them but never override another phone's. The server and its
Access secrets, the session, Update notifications and Usage stats stay on the phone
("start saving settings, both on the mobile app and also sync it": Tavi, 16 Oct 12:47).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] data-server-is-the-source
The private Inbox, diffs, tours and AI work MUST come from the configured server's API,
the same actions the web app runs. Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 anonymous browsing decision permits
the separate shared Explore client to call fixed HTTPS api.github.com REST GETs for
public repository discovery and PR lists without any private credentials or cache.
The phone MUST NOT call model providers or use an operator/personal token for Explore.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] data-ai-work-notice-follows-server
The app's ongoing AI notification MUST describe actual running analysis, tour, brief or
review tasks and derive elapsed time from the server's start timestamps, never an
estimate of progress. Completed, failed and cancelled tasks MUST leave it, and other
running tasks MUST remain. Observation MUST continue across page changes, clear on
sign-out or a server/account change, and MUST NOT ask for notification permission on
unrelated startup (Tavi's 20 Oct request to explore an app notification showing ongoing
tour generation and PR analysis with elapsed time).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] data-ai-work-notice-is-bounded
Ongoing AI progress notifications MUST expire without a fresh server snapshot, including after process
death or a lost connection. Background observation MUST be bounded and MUST NOT start a
foreground service solely to observe server work; reopening the app reattaches to actual
work (bounded implementation of Tavi's 20 Oct app-notification exploration). Separate
completion/failure alerts for explicitly owned tasks MAY remain until dismissed; their
durable ownership is bounded independently (Tavi, 21 Oct notification expansion).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] data-lite-diffs
A large pull request opens from a `lite` diff: files past the patch budget arrive with no
hunks and `patchOmitted`, show skeletons where their code goes, and get their hunks from
`diff-patches` (rules 51 and 52; architecture, The phone reads the server's store).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] data-tours-are-kept
Tours the person has opened are stored on the phone, so they open at once the next time
(CHANGELOG 0.28.0).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] data-jev-polls-briefly
While Inbox rows lack Jev's read and the Inbox needs it, the phone reads `my-pulls-cached`
with `revalidate: false` and `classify: true` every three seconds for two minutes at most,
and never shows a loading screen for it (architecture, Jev; rule 51).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] data-file-marks-follow-the-head
The phone drops a diff's file marks when the pull request's head moves, and shows Jev's
read only for the current head and title (architecture, Jev).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] data-posts-selected-critique-revision
Posting findings MUST send the displayed critique's variant, immutable revision and
head SHA with its selected IDs. A newer displayed result MUST reset selection, and a
late post of an older result MUST NOT mark the new result posted (repository review
15 Oct 2026, finding 8).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] data-analytics-queue-on-disk
Every usage event the phone tracks MUST be written to `filesDir/analytics/queue.ndjson`
as well as kept in memory, so no network and a killed app lose nothing: a crash's own
event is written to that file on the crashing thread, and what is left goes up on the
next start or with a WorkManager job that waits for a network. The queue keeps at most
5,000 events, dropping the oldest, and sends them to `POST /api/events` on the server set
in Settings, with the same Access headers as `/api/rpc`, at most 200 a call. It MUST NOT
use any analytics, crash or telemetry package (message 15 Oct 20:58, "We will track them
directly on our server. No need for fancy packages", and 21:12, "doit"; plan "Pulls
analytics on our own server").
In the anonymous Explore entry mode, private analytics MUST be paused without changing
the saved Usage stats choice or discarding a returning account's queued events. Guest
startup and workers MUST NOT send events to an unverified/private server. Source:
Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 ordinary signed-out browsing and isolated guest-authority decision.
Guest intervals MUST NOT later enter private screen/foreground durations, and a
private entry reached after guest startup MUST NOT be counted as a slow app launch
(22 Oct 2026 Compound guest review).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] data-analytics-counts-not-content
An event's props MUST carry only counts, timings, fixed choices, on or off values and a
pull request's repository and number. The phone MUST NOT send a file's name or path (a
file is its extension only), search or Ask text, a diff, code, a comment, an AI answer, a
title, a server address or any credential, and it drops every prop key the server would
drop (`AnalyticsRules.cleanProps`) before the event is queued. A screen is one of a fixed
set of lowercase words and a server call is its RPC name only, never its arguments. A
crash or a failed load carries only the error's class, its own message cut short, the top
frames of its stack and the screen (plan "Pulls analytics on our own server",
Guardrails; message 15 Oct 20:58).
